v 3
d datadeposit: prepare data and documentation for colleagues the way a data archive would
d
d datadeposit is for teams that work in Stata, R, and Python at once. It writes
d the kind of folder that archives such as ICPSR and Harvard Dataverse
d distribute: the data as csv plus Stata and R copies, a codebook (Markdown,
d Excel, DDI Codebook 2.5, Frictionless datapackage.json), and setup scripts
d that rebuild the labelled data from the csv in Stata, R, and Python.
d Variable labels, value labels, extended missing codes, notes, label
d languages, and survey question text stored in characteristics are all
d carried along. It reads Stata, delimited text, Excel, and SPSS files by
d content, and a size check stops deposits with files over 5 GB unless you
d choose lean (native file plus csv), nodata, or allowlarge.
d
d The same command exists in R and Python; all three write the same folder.
d
d Start with: help datadeposit
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth
d Support: email eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Version: 0.1.1
d Distribution-Date: 20261112
